 "narrative": {
  "northStar": "The day as a banknote",
  "overview": "Every kind of time is a denomination with its own ink, the way each Egyptian pound note carries its colour. The ground is pale security paper, the inks are intaglio colours (oxblood, madder, plum, sepia, ochre), and the shell around the app is a solid oxblood band. The world lends type, palette, density and one signature move; layout, navigation and controls stay the standard ones for a phone app.\n\nIt is used mostly outdoors in daylight, so the light theme is primary and every ink holds AA contrast on paper and on its own tint. A dark theme follows the OS for night review.",
  "keyCharacteristics": [
   "Oxblood shell: bottom bar on phones, side rail from 960px.",
   "Category inks on a 9% tint of themselves for each block row.",
   "Hour amounts set as large Spectral denomination numerals at the end of each row.",
   "The guilloche rosette as ميزان اليوم and ميزان الأسبوع.",
   "Fine one-pixel line work only; no ornament, no glow."
  ],
  "rules": [
   {
    "name": "The Denomination Rule",
    "body": "A category's ink is its identity everywhere: row tint, check circle, denomination numeral, week strip segment and rosette petals. Never use a category ink for anything that is not that category.",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Two Halves Rule",
    "body": "University and course form one half of the balance, work and life the other. New categories must join one half.",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Isolated Number Rule",
    "body": "Hour amounts with fractions (1½, 8¼) are wrapped in LTR isolates so they never reorder inside Arabic text.",
    "section": "typography"
   }
  ],
  "dos": [
   "Do keep every category ink at AA on paper and on its own 9% tint.",
   "Do show amounts of time as denominations, not as progress rings.",
   "Do keep line work at one pixel."
  ],
  "donts": [
   "Don't add Islamic ornament, mosque or Mushaf motifs.",
   "Don't use neon, glow or gradients.",
   "Don't reuse the retired palette (blue, violet, amber, green on blue-grey).",
   "Don't use a category ink for decoration."
  ]
 }
}